Names, not fetches
description: a URI is an identity — how it is reached is configuration, never part of the name
- >
  yamlover URIs are global and virtual — **identities, not fetch instructions** — like an AWS ARN: a
  pure colon-chained name. A `*` never performs a network request; the world-scope authority (`*:::
  pet.store.com: pets`) is a namespace tag resolved against the local mount table, and an unmounted
  authority simply yields nothing, with an "external" diagnostic.
- >
  Schemes, ports, and slash-paths are gone from the identifier: *how* an engine reaches a project is
  engine configuration, never part of the name. What remains is the scope ladder — more colons, wider
  scope — with a DNS-style authority naming an external project (the [scopes
  subchapter](::language:pointers:scopes)).
